*Core Library* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

The Chippy core library (corelib) is a comprehensive collection of libraries written in Chip that abstracts interpreter primitives to provide convenient, high-level functionality for common programming tasks.

Unlike builtins, which are implemented in Go and available automatically, core library modules must be explicitly loaded using ''load()'', see ''combine''.

The core library is installed under ''/usr/lib/chippy/'' and contains all necessary documentation. The source code for the core library can be found in the Chippy source tree under ''lib/''.
